CAT = "s7Accounts"; SEG = "ACC"
Q = [
("Under the customer identification program, which item must a firm obtain before opening an account for an individual?",
 "Date of birth", ["Annual income", "Employer's name", "Investment objective"],
 "The CIP rule requires name, date of birth, residential address and an identification number. Income, employment and objectives are gathered for suitability under FINRA rules, not CIP."),
("A new retail customer declines to name a trusted contact person when opening a cash account. The firm should:",
 "Open the account and note the request", ["Refuse to open the account", "List the rep as the trusted contact", "Allow only unsolicited trades"],
 "FINRA Rule 4512 requires only a reasonable effort to obtain a trusted contact. A customer may decline and the account can still be opened; a rep or other associated person may not serve as the trusted contact."),
("Two spouses open a joint account and want the survivor to receive the whole account at death. They should choose:",
 "Joint tenants with right of survivorship", ["Tenants in common with equal ownership shares", "A custodial account under UTMA", "A community property account"],
 "In JTWROS each owner has an undivided interest, and the survivor takes the deceased owner's share. In tenants in common the deceased's share goes to the estate."),
("Two brothers own an account as tenants in common, 70% and 30%. The 30% owner dies. His share goes to:",
 "His estate", ["The surviving brother", "The 70% owner's heirs", "A court-named custodian"],
 "Tenants in common owners hold separate interests that pass through each owner's estate. Only JTWROS sends the share straight to the survivor."),
("In a UTMA account for a minor, who is the owner of the securities for tax purposes?",
 "The minor", ["The custodian", "The parent who gave the gift", "The firm holding the account"],
 "Assets in a custodial account belong to the minor and are reported under the minor's Social Security number. The custodian manages them but cannot use them for personal benefit."),
("Which document is required to open a discretionary account?",
 "Written trading authorization", ["A notarized copy of the customer's will", "A signed margin agreement", "A signed loan consent form"],
 "Discretion over the asset, the action or the amount requires the customer's prior written authorization and principal acceptance. A margin agreement is needed only for margin."),
("On Monday morning a customer tells a rep to buy 500 shares of a named stock, leaving only price and timing to the rep. With no other written instruction, this authority lasts until:",
 "The close of that trading day", ["The end of that week", "The order is filled, however long", "Thirty days have passed"],
 "Time and price discretion needs no written authorization when the customer sets the security, action and amount, but under FINRA Rule 3260 it is limited to the day it is given unless the customer specifies otherwise in a signed, dated writing."),
("An employee of another FINRA member firm wants to open an account at your firm. Under Rule 3210, the employee must first:",
 "Obtain written consent from the employer", ["Get approval from FINRA", "Open the new account as a discretionary account", "Deposit at least $25,000"],
 "Rule 3210 requires prior written consent from the employing member before an associated person opens an account at another firm. The employer may ask for duplicate statements."),
("Which agreement must a customer sign before a firm will extend credit in a margin account?",
 "The credit agreement", ["The loan consent", "The options agreement", "The trusted contact form"],
 "The credit agreement explains how interest is charged. The hypothecation agreement lets the firm pledge the securities, while the loan consent, allowing the firm to lend them, is optional."),
("A principal approves a new options account on March 3. The options disclosure document had to reach the customer no later than:",
 "March 3", ["March 18", "April 2", "March 10"],
 "The ODD must be delivered at or before approval of the account for options trading. The 15-day window (March 18) applies to returning the signed options agreement."),
("A customer opening a new options account must return the signed options agreement:",
 "Within 15 days of account approval", ["Before account approval", "Within 30 days of the first trade", "Before writing uncovered calls"],
 "FINRA Rule 2360 requires the signed options agreement within 15 days after approval. If it does not arrive, the customer may only close existing positions."),
("For a corporate account, which document shows who may trade for the corporation?",
 "The corporate resolution", ["The articles of incorporation", "The corporation's bylaws", "The prior year's audit"],
 "The corporate resolution names the officers authorized to trade. A charter is also needed for a corporate margin account, to show the corporation may borrow and buy on margin."),
("A rep learns that a 78-year-old customer is likely being financially exploited. Under FINRA Rule 2165 the firm may:",
 "Place a temporary hold on disbursements", ["Close the account immediately", "Move assets to the trusted contact", "Freeze all of the customer's trades"],
 "Rule 2165 lets a firm place a temporary hold on disbursements of funds or securities from a specified adult's account when exploitation is reasonably believed, and it must notify the parties and investigate."),
("When a customer in an individual account dies, the rep's first step is to:",
 "Cancel open orders and freeze the account", ["Sell all positions at the market price", "Transfer all assets to the surviving spouse", "Close the account and mail a check to the estate"],
 "The account is frozen and open orders are cancelled until the executor provides documents such as a death certificate and letters testamentary. No one can trade without that authority."),
("Which setup is allowed for a UGMA custodial account?",
 "One adult for one minor", ["Two parents jointly", "The minor with a parent", "Any relative over 16"],
 "A custodial account has one custodian and one minor. Joint custodians and joint minors are not allowed."),
("A customer refuses to give her annual income when opening a cash account. The firm:",
 "May open it based on other information", ["Must refuse to open the account", "Must report her refusal to FinCEN", "Must open it only as a margin account"],
 "A customer may decline to supply financial information. The firm can open the account if it has enough other information to judge whether recommendations are suitable, and notes the refusal."),
]
